# Project Structure

## Overview

This document describes the structure and organization of the project.

## Directory Structure

```
src/
├── access/                    # Access functions for payload collections
├── app/                    # Next.js app directory
│   ├── (landing-page)/    # Landing page route group
│   ├── (payload)/           # Payload route group
├── collections/            # Payloadcms collection definitions
├── lib/                # Shared utility functions and types
├── migrations/              # Database migrations
├── resources/              # Translation resources
├── components/            # Shared components
│   ├── landing-page/     # Landing page specific components
│   └── ui/              # Reusable UI components
├── lib/                  # Utility functions and shared logic
└── resources/           # Static resources and translations
```

## File Naming Conventions

All file names in the project must use kebab-case (lowercase with hyphens). This applies to:

- Component files (e.g., `photo-grid.tsx`, `navigation-button.tsx`)
- Utility files (e.g., `date-utils.ts`, `string-helpers.ts`)
- Test files (e.g., `photo-grid.test.tsx`)
- Configuration files (e.g., `next.config.js`)

Examples:

- ✅ `photo-grid.tsx`
- ✅ `navigation-button.tsx`
- ✅ `featured-videos.tsx`
- ❌ `PhotoGrid.tsx` (PascalCase)
- ❌ `photoGrid.tsx` (camelCase)
- ❌ `photo_grid.tsx` (snake_case)

This convention helps maintain consistency across the codebase and follows common web development practices.

